WEBVTT

00:00:59.514 --> 00:01:02.183
Then, right when we enter the workforce,

00:01:02.225 --> 00:01:04.352
the answer becomes "no."

00:01:05.228 --> 00:01:08.189
The good news is
things look up again

00:01:08.231 --> 00:01:09.440
around 80.

00:01:09.482 --> 00:01:12.777
(Laughter)

00:01:13.152 --> 00:01:16.531
The bad news is the average
life expectancy is 78.

00:01:16.823 --> 00:01:17.990
So ...

00:01:18.032 --> 00:01:19.033
(Laughter)

00:01:19.075 --> 00:01:20.827
JA: It's not good
NB: It's not great.

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:22.328
JA: I’m a behavioral scientist

00:01:22.328 --> 00:01:25.832
who spent my career studying
what actually creates happiness in life

00:01:25.873 --> 00:01:27.375
versus what we think.

00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:29.043
NB: And I'm a corporate strategist

00:01:29.043 --> 00:01:33.005
who spent my career straddling
the worlds of business and improv comedy.